    <commands>
        <comment>
            Execute a command stream located at [offset, offset+size] of resourceId.

            This allows zero-copy execution as well as parallel execution.

            TODO: this is a strawman
        </comment>
        <command>
            <proto><type>void</type> <name>vnExecuteCommandStream</name></proto>
            <param><type>uint32_t</type> <name>executionId</name></param>
            <param><type>VkFlags</type> <name>flags</name></param>
            <param><type>VnResourceId</type> <name>resourceId</name></param>
            <param><type>size_t</type> <name>offset</name></param>
            <param><type>size_t</type> <name>size</name></param>
            <param><type>uint32_t</type> <name>dependencyCount</name></param>
            <param>const <type>uint32_t</type>* <name>dependencies</name></param>
        </command>

        <comment>
            A command can generate a reply to the reply stream when
            VN_COMMAND_GENERATE_REPLY_BIT is set. Such commands must be
            enclosed by vnBeginReplyStream and vnEndReplyStream.

            There can be multiple active reply streams when multiple command
            streams are executed in parallel.

            TODO: this is a strawman
        </comment>
        <command>
            <proto><type>void</type> <name>vnBeginReplyStream</name></proto>
            <param><type>VnResourceId</type> <name>resourceId</name></param>
            <param><type>size_t</type> <name>offset</name></param>
            <param><type>size_t</type> <name>size</name></param>
        </command>
        <command>
            <proto><type>void</type> <name>vnEndReplyStream</name></proto>
            <param><type>uint32_t</type> <name>dummy</name></param>
        </command>
    </commands>

